From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Thomas Karpiniec <tom.karpiniec@outlook.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 10:00:00 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: monaco-evk: enable the M.2 USB path

The M.2 Bluetooth USB connection is behind port 4 of the GL3590 hub.
Select the hub path for both USB speeds, release its reset and run the
primary controller as host. Without these GPIO settings, switching the
controller to host exposes only its root hubs, leaving Intel Bluetooth
unreachable even with btusb and firmware installed.

Adapt the routing and reset GPIOs from Swati Agarwal's Qualcomm host-mode
proposal to monaco-evk.dts, keeping other Monaco carriers unchanged. The
secondary controller remains available for the USB2 gadget port; WendyOS
must select a400000.usb instead of a600000.usb on this board.

Link: https://lore.kernel.org/all/20260430142000.3707614-1-swati.agarwal@oss.qualcomm.com/
Upstream-Status: Pending [board-scoped adaptation of the linked Qualcomm proposal]
Signed-off-by: Thomas Karpiniec <tom.karpiniec@outlook.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/monaco-evk.dts | 27 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 27 insertions(+)

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/monaco-evk.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/monaco-evk.dts
@@ -110 +110,28 @@
 };
+
+&expander5 {
+	usb1-ss-select-hog {
+		gpio-hog;
+		gpios = <5 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
+		output-high;
+	};
+};
+
+&tlmm {
+	usb1-hub-reset-hog {
+		gpio-hog;
+		gpios = <7 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
+		output-high;
+	};
+
+	usb1-hs-select-hog {
+		gpio-hog;
+		gpios = <14 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
+		output-high;
+	};
+};
+
+/* USB1 feeds the hub and M.2; USB2 remains available for the gadget. */
+&usb_1 {
+	dr_mode = "host";
+};
--
